   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to dental assisting practice",
    "basePrintNo": "S8533",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8533-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6608, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8533\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to dental assisting prac-\ntice\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to dental assisting practice\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 6608 of the education law to expand the prac-\ntices of registered dental assistants by allowing for the placing and\nremoval of temporary restorations while under the supervision of a\nlicensed dentist.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will expand dental assistants' scope of practice by allowing\nthem to place and remove temporary restorations under the supervision of\na licensed dentist. Being a very common occurrence in dental offices,\nthis amendment will help alleviate any pressure off of the dentist to\nperform these restorations, while still having oversight of the proce-\ndure. This legislation will allow dental offices to function more effi-\nciently, thereby benefiting the patient and allowing dentists and dental\nassistants to provide greater access to care.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
